      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Frequency domain correlative cardiogram (FCG) is a relatively new noninvasive method for diagnosis of coronary heart disease. However there has been little information about the application of FCG in pilots. To explore whether the FCG diagostic standards of normal people, can be applied to healthy pilots, 151 male pilots aged 22-47 (mean = 30 +/- 6 years) were examined with the HBD-II A instrument manufactured by Hong Kong WEX company. The results showed that the characteristics of FCG graph of the pilots were similar to that of the common healthy men. It indicates that the diagnostic standard of FCG for normal people can be used to pilots, so it might be useful in selection and real-time medical monitoring during ground training."},
